      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I didn't want to make a new canny since this existed already, so I'll add my findings to this post.\n\nWhen I am currently logged in to VRChat and I upload an avatar to a new blueprint ID, I can effectively recreate this issue. Avatars do not seem to update on the main menu page when they are uploaded while you are logged in.\n\nIf you upload, and then log in/launch the app, the uploaded avatars list is updated correctly.\n\nIf you have uploaded an avatar to a new blueprint ID while being logged in and you cannot see the avatar on your uploaded avatars list, then you can force it to refresh by looking at your uploaded avatars list in any of the wing menus.\n\nIf this logic already exists on the wing menus to update accordingly, then it should be easy to replicate that logic to the main menu area.\n\nI hope this helps with recreating and resolving the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
